<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">State of East Indonesia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1946–1950</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Negara Indonesia Timur</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The State of East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> was a federal state created by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> in December 1946 at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denpasar">Denpasar</a> Conference, covering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi">Sulawesi</a>, the Lesser <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunda-strait">Sunda</a> Islands and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maluku-islands">Moluccas</a>, with its capital at Makassar. It became a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> of Indonesia in December 1949, but popular pressure for a unitary republic grew, and it was dissolved into the Republic of Indonesia in 1950.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/state-of-east-indonesia.jpg" alt="State of East Indonesia" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dre.comandante · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_State_of_East_Indonesia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
